<title>PHILIPPINES: APEC leaders kick off summit talks.</title>
<headline>APEC leaders kick off summit talks.</headline>
<dateline>SUBIC BAY, Philippines 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Asia-Pacific leaders began their annual summit on Monday to draw up plans to create the 21st century's biggest free-trade community.</p>
<p>Leaders from the 18-member Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) forum, including U.S. President Bill Clinton, Chinese President Jiang Zemin and Japanese Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto, entered a conference hall at this former U.S. naval base to begin formal and informal discussions.</p>
</text>
